{"title":"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the number of degrees in the smaller angle between the hour hand and the minute hand on a clock that reads seven o'clock?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/9/ed9a4a4d1a78fa928e3856e1c0c38ea5ace08cd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 50^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 120^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 135^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 150^\\circ \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 165^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"449\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d081d4abf76b9d6c31b5af9693eba04731731ed9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0), 6)); dot((0,0)); draw((0,0)--(0,4)); draw((0,0)--(-1.5, -1.5*sqrt(3))); label(&quot;12&quot;, (0,5)); label(&quot;7&quot;, (-2.5, -2.5*sqrt(3))); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>The minute hand points at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> while the hour hand points at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Therefore, the angle between the hands is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/1/261d308e7ccf29a46d69981bb97112ce6bd7326b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of a full circle, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa3d488cc4a85f99e9058ee7aa7a7f7f1fc2adc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{12}\\cdot 360^\\circ = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 150^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"178\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME\" title=\"1989 AJHSME\">1989 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\